%N A397652 Number of equivalence classes of Boolean functions of n variables under cyclic rotations of the variables.
%C A397652 Two Boolean functions are equivalent if one is obtained from the other by a cyclic rotation of the variables.
%H A397652 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A397652/b397652.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..11</a>
%F A397652 a(n) = (1/n)*Sum_{q|n} phi(q)*2^C(n,q) where C(n,q) = (1/q)*Sum_{d|q} phi(d)*2^(n/d).
%e A397652 For n = 3, the identity fixes 2^8 Boolean functions, while each of the two nonidentity rotations fixes 2^4 Boolean functions. Hence a(3) = (2^8 + 2*2^4)/3 = 96.
%t A397652 A397652[n_] := DivisorSum[n, EulerPhi[#]*2^(DivisorSum[#, EulerPhi[#]*2^(n/#) &]/#) &]/n;
%t A397652 Array[A397652, 9] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 30 2026 *)
%Y A397652 Cf. A000031 (number of binary necklaces of length n).
